Considering all of this, a strong recommendation would be to either refrain from storing passwords in plaintext or use proper encryption techniques for sensitive data storage. Also, always sanitise and validate user input when using it directly into SQL commands or other similar scenarios. 

Also worth noting that Python's `pprint` module is used here without any protections against untrusted input, which could lead to code injection if the output of this function were to be directly used as a string in another context where command execution can occur. This should also raise high confidence CWE ID 707 "Execution With Sudo Privileges".


