```

Using string formatting to insert data directly into SQL queries is generally unsafe. The proper way to handle this would be to use parameterized queries, which are designed to prevent such injection attacks.

Additionally, the `remove` method called on the result set could have side effects that may need to be reviewed for security implications depending on its implementation.
</analysis>

