#### 6. CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)
**Finding:** The code does not appear to include any CSRF protection mechanisms.
**Reasoning:** The absence of anti-CSRF tokens in forms or requests can lead to CSRF attacks, where an attacker forces a user to execute unintended actions on a web application.
