CWEs: CWE-78 (OS Command Injection) - High Confidence, CWE-502 (Deserialization of Untrusted Data) - Low Confidence, CWE-120 (Buffer Overflow) - Low Confidence, CWE-20 (Path Traversal) - Low Confidence, CWE-287 (Improper Authentication) - Low Confidence

The most critical issue here is the OS Command Injection vulnerability due to `shell=True` in `subprocess.Popen`. This should be addressed immediately by avoiding shell injection or using safer methods for executing commands. For example, passing the command and its arguments as a list rather than a single string can help mitigate this risk.
</analysis>

