```
This could potentially result in the deletion of all records from the table.

The code also demonstrates poor practices regarding the use of string formatting for constructing SQL queries, which can lead to injection vulnerabilities even if the `idNormalizer` process_string method is supposed to sanitize the input. It is generally recommended to use parameterized queries or prepared statements instead of string formatting.

No other obvious security issues were found in this code snippet related to common CWEs within the given scope.
</analysis>

