While there is no direct concatenation of user input into SQL queries, the code uses string interpolation for building URLs and query parameters. Improper sanitization of these parameters could potentially lead to SQL injection if they are used in SQL queries downstream. However, further analysis would be required to confirm this vulnerability as it's not immediately apparent from this code block.
