   This line constructs a command that unpacks a file using `tar`. If an attacker can control the value of `filename`, they could inject malicious commands into the tar command. For example, if `filename` is set to something like `'file.tar; rm -rf /'`, it would result in the execution of `rm -rf /`, which is a severe security risk.

