Although not immediately apparent, this function stores user-controlled data (`host_name`) without proper encoding or escaping. This could lead to issues if the stored host name contains special characters that are interpreted by the storage system.

To mitigate these risks, consider implementing proper input validation and sanitization for `host_name`, using parameterized queries or prepared statements when executing SSH commands, and ensuring secure logging practices.
